'' 'cast( string, x )' over a UDT casting to string IS A STRING, so as the initializer of a
'' pointer, a number or an unrelated UDT it is fbc's error 24 -- measured on fbc-modern 1.20, lines
'' 12 to 18. It had no type, so nothing judged it and the statement stopped on TKO0994.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -c tests/diagnostics/src/cast-string-udt-init.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: cast-string-udt-init.bas(12,26): error TKO0653
'' EXPECT-OUT: cast-string-udt-init.bas(13,20): error TKO0653
'' EXPECT-OUT: cast-string-udt-init.bas(14,17): error TKO0653
'' EXPECT-OUT: cast-string-udt-init.bas(15,13): error TKO0653
'' EXPECT-OUT: cast-string-udt-init.bas(16,15): error TKO0653
'' EXPECT-OUT: cast-string-udt-init.bas(17,11): error TKO0738
'' EXPECT-OUT: cast-string-udt-init.bas(18,26): error TKO0653
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0994
